       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This totals 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the intended amount.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it. If you do intend 2550 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also like to know the clinical rationale so I can add it to the order note."
